@baseUrl = http://localhost:9001

# The Figma "Send to Ogen" plugin, end to end.
#
# Pairing: the plugin opens a pairing (unauthenticated), the signed-in user
# approves its write key in the web app (cookie auth — run "Login" from
# sessions/sessions.http first), then the plugin's poll with its read key
# collects the ogp_ token exactly once. Every /api/plugins/figma/* call after
# that sends "Authorization: Bearer <token>"; cookies are ignored there.
# Set postId (e.g. from posts/posts.http) for the attach flow.

### 1. Plugin: open a pairing
# @name startPairing
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/plugins/figma/pairings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "client_label": "Figma · Jane Doe"
}

> {%
client.global.set("readKey", response.body.read_key);
client.global.set("writeKey", response.body.write_key);
%}

### 2. Plugin: poll before approval (expects 202 {"status":"pending"})
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plugins/figma/pairings/{{readKey}}

### 3. Web app: preview the pairing on the approval page  [protected]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/integrations/figma/pairings/{{writeKey}}
Accept: application/json

### 4. Web app: allow it — binds to the active workspace (add X-Workspace-Id to pick one)  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/integrations/figma/pairings/{{writeKey}}/approve
Accept: application/json

> {% client.global.set("connectionId", response.body.connection.id); %}

### 4b. ALTERNATIVE to 4 — skip it in a normal run (after 4 it answers 409 pairing_not_pending). Deny; the next poll gets 403 pairing_denied  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/integrations/figma/pairings/{{writeKey}}/deny

### 5. Plugin: collect the token (200 once; 410 pairing_expired after)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plugins/figma/pairings/{{readKey}}

> {% client.global.set("pluginToken", response.body.token); %}

### 6. Plugin: who am I
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plugins/figma/me
Authorization: Bearer {{pluginToken}}

### 7. Plugin: draft-post picker
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plugins/figma/posts?q=&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{pluginToken}}

### 7b. Plugin: "Send to" picker — live campaigns with their posts (all statuses; attachable=false once submitted)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plugins/figma/campaigns
Authorization: Bearer {{pluginToken}}

### 8. Plugin: send a frame to the content bank
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/plugins/figma/images
Authorization: Bearer {{pluginToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="node_id"

12:345
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="node_name"

Hero / Desktop
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file_name"

Launch campaign
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="hero.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./sample.png
--boundary--

### 9. Plugin: send a frame and attach it to a post (attach_error explains a refusal; the asset is kept)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/plugins/figma/images
Authorization: Bearer {{pluginToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="node_id"

12:346
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="node_name"

Hero / Mobile
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="post_id"

{{postId}}
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="alt_text"

Product hero on a phone screen
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="hero-mobile.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./sample.png
--boundary--

### 9b. Plugin: start sending a rendered video to a post (MP4 or WebM; size_bytes = the export's byte length)
# Needs a short MP4 at ./sample.mp4 (not committed). Steps 9b-9d run as one unit.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/plugins/figma/posts/{{postId}}/videos/presign
Authorization: Bearer {{pluginToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content_type": "video/mp4",
  "size_bytes": 1048576
}

> {%
client.global.set("videoUploadUrl", response.body.upload_url);
client.global.set("videoKey", response.body.s3_key);
%}

### 9c. Plugin: PUT the bytes straight to storage (no Authorization header; same Content-Type)
PUT {{videoUploadUrl}}
Content-Type: video/mp4

< ./sample.mp4

### 9d. Plugin: attach the uploaded video (repeat it: 200 with the same attachment)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/plugins/figma/posts/{{postId}}/videos/finalize
Authorization: Bearer {{pluginToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "s3_key": "{{videoKey}}",
  "node_id": "12:347",
  "node_name": "Hero / Reel",
  "file_name": "Launch campaign"
}

### 10. Web app: list plugin connections (own; owners see everyone's)  [protected]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/integrations/figma/connections
Accept: application/json

### 11. Web app: disconnect a plugin  [protected]
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/integrations/figma/connections/{{connectionId}}

### 12. Plugin: disconnect itself
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/plugins/figma/token
Authorization: Bearer {{pluginToken}}

### 13. Plugin: any call with a revoked token (expects 401 plugin_token_invalid)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plugins/figma/me
Authorization: Bearer {{pluginToken}}
